## Issue Description

When using Impit for HTTP requests, the response headers returned from `impit.fetch()` don't match the standard [`Headers`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Headers) interface provided by the Fetch API. This causes incompatibility with existing code that expects standard headers behavior.

## Details

- The headers object returned by Impit doesn't support methods like `getAll()`, which are required for properly processing Set-Cookie headers
- Response headers are returned as a plain object (Record<string, string | string[]>) rather than a standard Headers object
- Cookie handling is particularly affected since Set-Cookie headers need special processing

